            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a moneylender, then the Bengali for the rest (remaining)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: অভাব",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অভাব — ôbhāb — \"want; lack; need\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গরমে গ্রামে জলের অভাব হয়। gôrôme grāme jôler ôbhāb hôy. In summer the village runs short of water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also hardship itself: অভাবের দিন, hard times; টাকার অভাব (ôbhāb), a shortage of money."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "অভাব (ôbhāb) is Sanskrit abhāva, \"non-existence, absence\" (Monier-Williams), from a-, not, and bhāva, being; Bengali uses it for the want of what one needs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
