          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সম্বল (sômbôl) is Sanskrit śambala, also written sambala, \"provisions for a journey\" (Monier-Williams): পথের সম্বল keeps the old sense, and the word has grown to mean all one has to live on."
